Tier 1 -- pure unit tests (workstation, milliseconds).

The policy functions, kept out of the verbs so they are testable without a
system: snapshot-name parse/format/compare, staleness arithmetic, succession
resolution, quorum evaluation, retention-ladder selection. Table-driven, no
ZFS, no jails, no CBSD. See TESTING.md §2.

At M0 this tier holds only the harness's own self-test: proof that a failing
assertion is reported as "not ok" and exits non-zero.

Files named t_*.sh are tests. Anything else here (this README, future fixture
data) is ignored by tests/run.sh.
